# 005-switchpt-two-versions (v4): PumpAi SwitchPT treats the host as two creatures (forge-ai CODE patch, NOT applied)
# v4 = v3 + three changes (user order via Claude 2, 2026-10-22): the "only after blockers are declared" gate is skipped when the
# host attacks and no untapped creature of the defending player can block it (CombatUtil.canBlock; empty field or all
# blockers tapped/unable). Then the switch is allowed once attackers are declared (COMBAT_DECLARE_ATTACKERS), because blocks cannot
# change the outcome. Beginning of combat stays closed (the spam). Everything else as v3: at most 1 switch + 1 back per turn,
# versionScore via ComputerUtilCard.shouldPumpCard, discard cost must be beaten by the gain.
# v3 is archived in patches/archive/005-switchpt-two-versions-v3.patch. Test-only activation log: 015-switchpt-check-log.patch.
# Test (v3, 40 games, switch-heavy deck vs Sai): activations 356 -> 52, wins 5 vs 1 (n.s.); v4 not yet tested.
# (second change: when the early gate applies, switchPTHelps compares versionScore of the two versions instead of shouldPumpCard, which only predicts unblocked attackers after blockers are declared; found in the first 6-game run, helps=false at declare attackers.)
# (third change: PumpAi.checkApiLogic skips its own shouldPumpCard call for the early switch, otherwise it vetoed it again at declare attackers.)
